{\*\background{\shp{\*\shpinst\shpleft0\shptop0\shpright0\shpbottom0\shpfhdr0\shpbxmargin\shpbxignore\shpbymargin\shpbyignore\shpwr0\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt1\shplid1025{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fFlipH}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fFlipV}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fillColor}{\sv 16777215}}{\sp{\sn fFilled}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn lineWidth}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fLine}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fBackground}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}}}}\sectd
\headery567\footery567\pgwsxn12240\pghsxn15840\marglsxn1440\margtsxn1440\margrsxn1440\margbsxn1440\pgbrdropt32\pard\ltrpar\itap0\nowidctlpar\ql\li0\ri0\lin0\rin0\plain\rtlch\af0\afs20\alang16393\ltrch\f0\fs20\lang16393\langnp16393\langfe16393\langfenp16393 Is the data in the "Disclosure of complete set of financial statements [text block]" complete? \par\par The entire set of financial statements as used or tabled for purposes of the Annual General Meeting must be provided in this single text block of "Disclosure of complete set of financial statements [text block]".\par\par The information submitted within "Disclosure of complete set of financial statements [text block]" contains less than 5,000 characters.\par\par Disclosure of complete set of financial statements [text block] should contain the entire set of financial statements and it generally includes the following:\par -31-12-2024 register date\par - Directors' statement\par - Independent auditors' report (if financial statements are audited)\par - Statement of financial position\par - Statement of profit or loss and other comprehensive income\par - Statement of cash flows\par - Total assets, Liabilities, Equity\par - Profit (loss) before taxation, Profit (loss)\par - Notes, comprising of a summary of accounting policies and other explanatory information\par\par If the Company had obtained exemption from this rule in prior year, no exemption is required.\par\par Specific key words are noted to be missing from the "Disclosure of complete set of financial statements [text block]" when Property plant and equipment is reported.\par\par If the accounting standard used is "SFRS for SE", "Disclosure of complete set of financial statements [text block]" will generally indicate accordingly e.g. Singapore Financial Reporting Standard for Small Entities.\par\par Disclosure of complete set of financial statements [text block] should contain the entire set of financial statements and it generally includes the following:\par\par - Tabular data for Note- Property plant equipment\par - Net book value at end of period\par - Carrying value at end of period\par\par Specific key words are noted to be missing from the "Disclosure of complete set of financial statements [text block]".Disclosure of complete set of financial statements [text block] should contain the entire set of financial statements and it generally includes the following:\par - Directors' statement\par - Independent auditors' report (if financial statements are audited)\par - Statement of financial position\par - Statement of profit or loss and other comprehensive income\par - Statement of cash flows\par - Total assets, Liabilities, Equity\par - Profit (loss) before taxation, Profit (loss)\par - Notes, comprising of a summary of accounting policies and other explanatory information\par\par\par\par The entire set of financial statement as used or tabled for purposes of Annual General Meeting must be provided in this single text block of "Disclosure of complete set of financial statements "[text block]".\par\par Specific key words are noted to be missing from the "Disclosure of complete set of financial statements [text block]".\par\par Disclosure of complete set of financial statements [text block] should contain the entire set of financial statements and it generally includes the following:\par\par - Directors' statement\par - Independent auditors' report (if financial statements are audited)\par - Statement of financial position/ Balance sheet\par - Statement of profit or loss and other comprehensive income/ Income statement\par - Statement of changes in equity\par - Statement of cash flows\par - key words like total assets, total liabilities, total equity\par\par\par Report on Financial Statements\par We have audited the accompanying financial statements of Sanmar Foundries Limited ( the Company ), which comprise the balance sheet as at March 31, 2013, the statement of profit and loss and cash flow statement for the year then ended, a summary of significant accounting policies and other explanatory information.\par\par Managements  Responsibility for the Financial Statements\par Management is responsible for the preparation of these financial statements that give a true and fair view of the financial position, financial performance and cash flows of the Company in accordance with the Accounting Standards referred to in sub-section (3C) of section 211 of the Companies Act, 1956 ( the Act ). This responsibility includes the design, implementation and maintenance of internal control relevant to the preparation and presentation of the financial statements that give a true and fair view and are free from material misstatement, whether due to fraud or error.\par\par Auditors  responsibility\par Our responsibility is to express an opinion on these financial statements based on our audit. We conducted our audit in accordance with the Standards on Auditing issued by the Institute of Chartered Accountants of India. Those Standards require that we comply with ethical requirements and plan and perform the audit to obtain reasonable assurance about whether the financial statements are free from material misstatement.\par\par An audit involves performing procedures to obtain audit evidence, about the amounts and disclosures in the financial statements. The procedures selected depend on the auditors  judgment, including the assessment of the risks of material misstatement of the financial statements, whether due to fraud or error.  In making those risk assessments, the auditors consider internal control relevant to the Company s preparation and fair presentation of the financial statements in order to design audit procedures that are appropriate in the circumstances.  An audit also includes evaluating the appropriateness of accounting policies used and the reasonableness of the accounting estimates made by the management, as well as evaluating the overall presentation of the financial statements.\par We believe that the audit evidence we have obtained is sufficient and appropriate to provide a basis for our audit opinion.\par\par Independent Auditor s Report \par Page 2 of 3\par Basis of qualified opinion: \par The Company has recognized Deferred Tax Assets ( DTA ) aggregating to Rs. 379,000,000 as at March 31, 2013 including an amount of Rs. 24,000,000 for the current year on business losses and unabsorbed depreciation based on profitability projections for the future and the consequent realization of the DTA. In our opinion, such basis of recognition is not in accordance with the requirements of virtual certainty under Accounting Standard 22- Income Taxes of the Companies (Accounting Standards) Rules 2006 (as amended). Had the aforesaid observation been considered and the entire DTA of Rs. 379,000,000 (Rs. 24,000,000 recognised in the current year and Rs. 355,000,000 recognised in earlier years) not been recognized in the current year, the net loss after tax for the year would have been Rs. 390,186,081 as against the reported net loss after tax for the year ended March 31, 2013 of Rs. 11,186,081 and reserves and surplus as at March 31, 2013 would have been lower by Rs.379,000,000. The audit report for the year ended March 31, 2012 was also qualified in respect of this matter.\par Opinion\par In our opinion, and to the best of our information and according to the explanations given to us, except for the effects of the matter described in the basis of qualified opinion paragraph, the financial statements give the information required by the Companies Act, 1956 in the manner so required and give a true and fair view in conformity with the accounting principles generally accepted in India:\par\par (a) in the case of the balance sheet, of the state of affairs of the Company as at March 31, 2013;\par\par (b) in the case of the statement of profit and loss, of the loss for the year ended on that date; and\par\par (c) in the case of the cash flow statement, of the cash flows for the year ended on that date.\par\par Report on other legal and regulatory requirements\par\par 1.As required by the Companies (Auditor's Report) Order, 2003 ( the Order ), as amended, issued by the Central Government of India in terms of sub-section (4A) of section 227 of the Companies Act, 1956, we enclose in the Annexure a statement on the matters specified in paragraphs 4 and 5 of the said Order.\par\par 2.Further to our comments in the Annexure referred to above, we report that: \par\par (a)We have obtained all the information and explanations which, to the best of our knowledge and belief, were necessary for the purpose of our audit;\par\par (b)In our opinion, proper books of account as required by law have been kept by the Company so far as appears from our examination of the books of account;\par Independent Auditor s Report \par To the Members of Sanmar Foundries Limited\par\par (c)The balance sheet, statement of profit and loss, and cash flow statement dealt with by this report are in agreement with the books of account;\par\par (d)  Except for the effects of the matter described in the basis of qualified opinion paragraph, the balance sheet, statement of profit and loss, and cash flow statement dealt with by this report comply with the accounting standards referred to in sub-section (3C) of section 211 of the Companies Act, 1956; and\par\par (e)On the basis of written representations received from the directors as at March 31 2013, and taken on record by the board of directors, we report that none of the directors is disqualified as at March 31 2013, from being appointed as a director in terms of clause (g) of sub-section (1) of section 274 of the Companies Act, 1956.}]]></sg-as:DisclosureOfCompleteSetOfFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
